<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Buknu> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Buknu** is a powdered [mixture of several spices](:Spice_mix) popular in parts of [Uttar Pradesh](:Uttar_Pradesh), [India](:India).Buknu is a very ancient recipe and is claimed to have medicinal values. It is used as both a spice and a condiment. Buknu's main ingredients include [amchoor](:Amchoor), [salt](:Salt), [turmeric](:Turmeric), [cumin seeds](:Cumin), [asafoetida](:Asafoetida), [black cumin](:Nigella_sativa), [black cardamom](:Black_cardamom), and [oil](:Cooking_oil).The recipe for Buknu likely originated in the Kanpur city of Uttar Pradesh."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
