<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Shooter's_sandwich> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **shooter's sandwich** is a [steak sandwich](:Steak_sandwich) consisting of cooked steak and mushrooms placed inside a hollowed-out loaf of bread and then weighted down. This popular English sandwich is likened to [beef Wellington](:Beef_Wellington) using bread rather than pastry.A shooter's sandwich is prepared by filling a long, hollowed-out loaf of bread with cooked [filet mignon](:Filet_mignon) steak, cooked mushrooms, salt, and pepper. Weights are then placed atop the sandwich to squeeze it down. Typically the sandwich is weighted down overnight, which causes meat juices to soak into the bread.Other cuts of beef, such as [rump steak](:Rump_steak), [ribeye](:Rib_eye_steak), and [sirloin](:Sirloin_steak) are also used to prepare the item. Cooked onions or shallots are sometimes used, as is [duxelles](:Duxelles), a sautéed preparation of mushrooms, onions or shallots, and herbs, reduced to a [paste](:Paste_%28food%29). [Dijon mustard](:Dijon_mustard) and [horseradish](:Horseradish%23Horseradish_sauce) are sometimes used as accompanying [condiments](:Condiment)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
