<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A spice is a seed, fruit, root, bark, or other plant substance primarily used for flavoring or coloring food. Spices are distinguished from herbs, which are the leaves, flowers, or stems of plants used for flavoring or as a garnish. Spices are sometimes used in medicine, religious rituals, cosmetics or perfume production. For example, vanilla is commonly used as an ingredient in fragrance manufacturing. Although health benefits are often claimed for spices, there is currently not enough research conducted to prove these benefits."@en .
