<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Fios_de_ovos> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Angel hair**, called in [Portuguese](:Portuguese_language) ***Fios de ovos*** (\"egg threads\") is a traditional [Portuguese](:Portugal) sweet food made of [eggs](:Egg_%28food%29) (chiefly [yolks](:Yolk%29), drawn into thin strands and boiled in [sugar](:Sugar) [syrup](:Syrup). They are a traditional element in [Portuguese](:Cuisine_of_Portugal) and [Brazilian cuisine](:Cuisine_of_Brazil), both in [desserts](:Dessert) and as [side dishes](:Side_dish) (only in Brazil).The preparation is also known in [Spain](:Spain) as ***Huevo hilado*** (\"[spun](:Spinning_%28textiles%29) egg\"), in [Japan](:Japan) as ***Keiran Somen*** (鶏卵素麺, \"hen's egg noodle\"), in [Cambodia](:Cambodia) as ***Vawee***, in Malaysia as ***Jala mas*** (\"golden net\"), in [Thailand](:Thailand) as ***Foi Thong*** (ฝอยทอง; \"golden strands\"), and in the [North Malabar](:North_Malabar) region of [Kerala, India](:Kerala%2C_India) as ***Muttamala*** (മുട്ടമാല; \"egg lace\")."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
