<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Soufflé> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A soufflé is a baked egg-based dish originating in France in the early eighteenth century. Combined with various other ingredients it can be served as a savory main dish or sweetened as a dessert. The word soufflé is the past participle of the French verb souffler which means \"to blow\", \"to breathe\", \"to inflate\" or \"to puff\"."@en .
