<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mint_(candy)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A **mint** or **breath mint** is a food item often consumed as an after-meal refreshment or before business and social engagements to improve breath odor. Mints are commonly believed to soothe the stomach given their association with natural byproducts of the plant genus *[Mentha](:Mentha)*. Mints sometimes contain derivatives from plants such as [peppermint](:Peppermint) oil or [spearmint](:Spearmint) oil, or [wintergreen](:Wintergreen) from the plant genus *[Gaultheria](:Gaultheria)*. However, many of the most popular mints citing these natural sources contain none in their ingredient list or contain only trace amounts."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
