<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ham> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Ham** is [pork](:Pork) from a leg [cut](:Cut_of_pork) that has been [preserved](:Food_preservation) by wet or dry [curing](:Curing_%28food_preservation%29), with or without [smoking](:Smoking_%28cooking%29). As a [processed meat](:Processed_meat), the term \"ham\" includes both whole cuts of meat and ones that have been mechanically formed.Ham is made around the world, including a number of regional specialties, such as [Westphalian ham](:Westphalian_ham) and some varieties of [Spanish *jamón*](:Jam%C3%B3n). In addition, numerous ham products have specific geographical naming protection, such as [prosciutto di Parma](:Prosciutto_di_Parma) in Europe, and [Smithfield ham](:Smithfield_ham) in the US."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
