<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lalanga> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Lalanga is a deep fried flatbread found in Greek and Turkish cuisines. Historically it was present in both Byzantine and Ottoman cuisines."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chocolate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Chocolate** is a [food](:Food) made from roasted and ground [cacao seed](:Cacao_seed) kernels that is available as a liquid, solid, or paste, either on its own or as a [flavoring agent](:Flavoring_agent) in other foods. Cacao has been consumed in some form since at least the [Olmec](:Olmec) civilization (19th-11th century BCE), and the majority of [Mesoamerican](:Mesoamerican) people ─ including the [Maya](:Maya_civilization) and [Aztecs](:Aztec) ─ made chocolate beverages.The seeds of the [cacao tree](:Cacao_tree) have an intense [bitter](:Bitter_%28taste%29) taste and must be [fermented](:Fermentation_%28food%29) to develop the flavor. After fermentation, the seeds are dried, cleaned, and roasted. The shell is removed to produce cocoa nibs, which are then ground to [cocoa mass](:Cocoa_mass), unadulterated chocolate in rough form. Once the cocoa mass is liquefied by heating, it is called [chocolate liquor](:Chocolate_liquor). The liquor may also be cooled and processed into its two components: [cocoa solids](:Cocoa_solids) and [cocoa butter](:Cocoa_butter). [Baking chocolate](:Baking_chocolate), also called bitter chocolate, contains cocoa solids and cocoa butter in varying proportions, without any [added sugar](:Added_sugar). Powdered baking cocoa, which contains more [fiber](:Dietary_fiber) than cocoa butter, can be processed with [alkali](:Alkali) to produce [dutch cocoa](:Dutch_process_chocolate). Much of the chocolate consumed today is in the form of [sweet chocolate](:Sweet_chocolate), a combination of cocoa solids, cocoa butter or added vegetable oils, and sugar. [Milk chocolate](:Milk_chocolate) is sweet chocolate that additionally contains [milk powder](:Milk_powder) or [condensed milk](:Condensed_milk). [White chocolate](:White_chocolate) contains cocoa butter, sugar, and milk, but no cocoa solids.Chocolate is one of the most popular food types and flavors in the world, and many foodstuffs involving chocolate exist, particularly [desserts](:Dessert), including [cakes](:Chocolate_cake), [pudding](:Chocolate_pudding), [mousse](:Chocolate_mousse), [chocolate brownies](:Chocolate_brownie), and [chocolate chip cookies](:Chocolate_chip_cookie). Many [candies](:Candy) are filled with or coated with sweetened chocolate. [Chocolate bars](:Chocolate_bar), either made of solid chocolate or other ingredients coated in chocolate, are eaten as [snacks](:Snack). Gifts of chocolate molded into different shapes (such as eggs, hearts, coins) are traditional on certain Western holidays, including [Christmas](:Christmas), [Easter](:Easter_egg%23Chocolate_eggs), [Valentine's Day](:Valentine%27s_Day), and [Hanukkah](:Hanukkah_gelt). Chocolate is also used in cold and hot beverages, such as [chocolate milk](:Chocolate_milk) and [hot chocolate](:Hot_chocolate), and in some alcoholic drinks, such as [creme de cacao](:Creme_de_cacao).Although cocoa originated in the Americas, [West African countries](:West_Africa), particularly [Côte d'Ivoire](:C%C3%B4te_d%27Ivoire) and [Ghana](:Ghana), are the leading producers of cocoa in the 21st century, accounting for some 60% of the world cocoa supply.With some two million [children involved in the farming of cocoa](:Child_labour_in_cocoa_production) in West Africa, [child slavery and trafficking](:Child_labour_in_cocoa_production%23Child_slavery_and_trafficking) associated with the cocoa trade remain major concerns. A 2018 report argued that international attempts to improve conditions for children were doomed to failure because of persistent poverty, absence of schools, increasing world cocoa demand, more [intensive farming](:Intensive_farming) of cocoa, and continued exploitation of child labor."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
