<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pinole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Pinole**, also called **pinol** or **[pinolillo](:Pinolillo),** is roasted ground maize, which is then mixed with a combination of cocoa, agave, cinnamon, chia seeds, vanilla, or other spices. The resulting powder is then used as a nutrient-dense ingredient to make different foods, such as cereals, baked goods, tortillas, and beverages. The name comes from the [Nahuatl](:Nahuatl) word *pinolli*, meaning cornmeal. Today, pinole is generally made by hand using wood-burning adobe ovens and a stone and pestle, and is still consumed in certain, often rural, parts of Latin America. Pinole is considered the national beverage of [Nicaragua](:Nicaragua) and [Honduras](:Honduras)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
