<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Jolada_rotti> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Jolada rotti** is an unleavened [Indian bread](:Indian_bread) made of [sorghum bicolor](:Sorghum_bicolor)It is coarser than a [roti](:Roti). It can be either soft or hard in texture, compared to a [khakhra](:Khakhra) or [cracker](:Cracker_%28food%29) with respect to hardness. The name literally translates as \"sorghum bread\".Jolada rotti is part of the [staple diet](:Staple_diet) of most of the [districts](:Districts_of_Karnataka) of North Karnataka, where it is eaten with [pulse](:Pulses) [curries](:Curry) such as [jhunka](:Jhunka), yengai, shenga chutney or other assorted [chutnies](:Chutney).Jowar rotti is also called as jawarichi [bhakri](:Bhakri) in neighboring [Maharastra](:Maharastra).  "^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
