<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Vienna_sausage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A Vienna sausage (German: Wiener Würstchen, Wiener; Viennese/Austrian German: Frankfurter Würstel or Würstl; Swiss German: Wienerli; Swabian: Wienerle or Saitenwurst) is a thin parboiled sausage traditionally made of pork and beef in a casing of sheep's intestine, then given a low temperature smoking. The word Wiener is German for Viennese. In Austria, the term \"Wiener\" is uncommon for this food item, which instead is usually called Frankfurter Würstl."@en .
