<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lulada> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Lulada** is a traditional [Colombian](:Colombian_cuisine) beverage from [Cali](:Cali), in the [Valle del Cauca Department](:Valle_del_Cauca_Department) of Colombia. It is prepared from [lulo](:Naranjilla), a fruit common to the region, lime juice, water, and sugar for sweetness. It often has the texture and consistency of a smoothie and is sometimes served with a shot of [aguardiente](:Aguardiente). A lulada differs from the standard lulo juice in that the lulo fruit is not blended during the drink's preparation."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
