<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cheese_in_Kenya> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Several companies make cheese in Kenya, though cheese is not a traditional Kenyan food, and the market is expanding. Cheese consumption has been increasing within the Kenyan middle-class. As of 2016 the five largest manufacturers of cheese in Kenya were Browns, active since the 1970s with 22% of the market; Raka, established 2001 with 19%; Dama Dairy established 1994, Happy Cow Kenya, Eldoville Dairies and New Kenya Co-operative Creameries (New KCC). Cheese produced in Kenya includes Cheddar, Gouda, blue cheese, feta, mascarpone, ricotta, mozzarella and brie."@en .
