<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cheese_in_Kenya> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Several companies make **cheese in Kenya**, though cheese is not a traditional Kenyan food, and the market is expanding. Cheese consumption has been increasing within the Kenyan middle-class.As of 2016[[update]](//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cheese_in_Kenya&action=edit) the five largest manufacturers of cheese in Kenya were Browns, active since the 1970s with 22% of the market; Raka, established 2001 with 19%; Dama Dairy established 1994, Happy Cow Kenya, Eldoville Dairies and New Kenya Co-operative Creameries (New KCC).Cheese produced in Kenya includes [Cheddar](:Cheddar_cheese), [Gouda](:Gouda_cheese), [blue cheese](:Blue_cheese), [feta](:Feta), [mascarpone](:Mascarpone), [ricotta](:Ricotta), [mozzarella](:Mozzarella) and [brie](:Brie)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
