<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Gising-gising> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Gising-gising, also known as ginataang sigarilyas, is a spicy Filipino vegetable soup or stew originating from the provinces of Nueva Ecija and Pampanga in the Philippines. It is traditionally made with chopped winged beans (sigarillas or sigarilyas), and coconut milk spiced with labuyo chili, garlic, onions, and bagoong alamang (shrimp paste). The name literally means \"wake up, wake up\". It can be eaten alone, on top of rice, or as a side dish to grilled meat dishes. It is a type of ginataan."@en .
