<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bologna_sausage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Bologna sausage, also spelled baloney (/bəˈloʊni/ bə-LOH-nee), is a sausage derived from the Italian mortadella, a similar-looking, finely ground pork sausage containing cubes of pork fat, originally from the city of Bologna (IPA: [boˈloɲɲa]). Typical seasonings for bologna include black pepper, nutmeg, allspice, celery seed and coriander, and, like mortadella, myrtle berries give it its distinctive flavor. In North America, a simple and popular use is in the bologna sandwich."@en .
