<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Shrimp_paste> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Shrimp paste** or **prawn sauce** is a [fermented](:Fermentation) condiment commonly used in [Southeast Asian](:Southeast_Asian_cuisine) and Southern [Chinese cuisines](:Chinese_cuisine). It is primarily made from finely crushed [shrimp](:Shrimp) or [krill](:Krill) mixed with salt, and then fermented for several weeks. They are either sold in their wet form or are sun-dried and either cut into rectangular blocks or sold in bulk. It is an essential ingredient in many [curries](:Curry), sauces and [sambal](:Sambal). Shrimp paste can be found in many meals in [Cambodia](:Cambodia), [Indonesia](:Indonesia), [Laos](:Laos), [Malaysia](:Malaysia), [Myanmar](:Myanmar), [the Philippines](:Philippines), [Singapore](:Singapore), [Thailand](:Thailand), and [Vietnam](:Vietnam). It is often an ingredient in [dip](:Dip_%28food%29) for fish or vegetables."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
