<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lunumiris> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Lunumiris** ([Sinhala](:Sinhalese_language):ලුණු මිරිස් [lunu-miris] means salt and chillies in Sinhalese. Traditionally it is made with ground chillies and salt mixed together into a paste. Some also refer it as \"Katta [Sambal](:Sambal)\" but Katta sambal or sambol has Maldive fish in the recipe along with shallots and salt. [Sinhala:කට්ට සම්බෝල [kaṭṭa sambōla]]) is a spicy [Sri Lankan](:Sri_Lanka) [sambal](:Sambal) paste served as a condiment. It consists of [chili pepper](:Chili_pepper), [shallots](:Shallot), [Maldive fish](:Maldive_fish), [sea salt](:Sea_salt), [black pepper](:Black_pepper) and [lime juice](:Lime_juice), usually ground with a [mortar and pestle](:Mortar_and_pestle) or a grind stone.This is a paste which is a little bit hot because of the [chili powder](:Chili_powder) added."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
