<http://dbpedia.org/resource/New_England-style_hot_dog_bun> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**New England-style hot dog buns**, also often known as **New England hot dog buns** or **top-loading hot dog buns**, are the [hot dog buns](:Hot_dog_bun) most commonly used in the [United States](:United_States) region of [New England](:New_England) and its [cuisine](:Cuisine_of_New_England). They may also be called **split-top**, **top-sliced**, **frankfurter rolls**, or **frankfurt rolls**."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
