<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Queijo_coalho> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***Queijo coalho*** or ***queijo-de-coalho*** (Template:IPA-pt, literally \"cheese curd\") is a firm but very lightweight [cheese](:Cheese) produced in [Northeastern Brazil](:Northeastern_Brazil), with an almost \"squeaky\" texture when bitten into (similar to [cheese curds](:Cheese_curd%29).It is a popular and cheap snack for beach-goers in Brazil or in homemade [churrasco](:Churrasco), where the cheese is cooked over a charcoal grill, often with a sprinkling of [oregano](:Oregano) or [garlic](:Garlic)-flavored sauce. It is eaten off a stick, much like a [kebab](:Kebab). It gets a golden surface when grilled, and does not melt much."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
