<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kaong_palm_vinegar> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Kaong palm vinegar**, also known as **irok palm vinegar** or **arengga palm vinegar**, is a traditional [Filipino](:Filipino_cuisine) [vinegar](:Vinegar) made from the [sap](:Sap) of the kaong sugar palm (*[Arenga pinnata](:Arenga_pinnata)*). It is one of the four main types of vinegars in the [Philippines](:Philippines), along with [coconut vinegar](:Coconut_vinegar), [cane vinegar](:Cane_vinegar), and [nipa palm vinegar](:Nipa_palm_vinegar). It is usually sold under the generic label of \"**palm vinegar**\"."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
