<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Gising-gising> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***Gising-gising***, also known as ***ginataang sigarilyas***, is a spicy [Filipino](:Cuisine_of_the_Philippines) [vegetable soup](:Vegetable_soup) or stew originating from the provinces of [Nueva Ecija](:Nueva_Ecija) and [Pampanga](:Pampanga) in the [Philippines](:Philippines). It is traditionally made with chopped [winged beans](:Winged_bean) (*sigarillas* or *sigarilyas*), and [coconut milk](:Coconut_milk) spiced with *[labuyo](:Siling_labuyo)* chili, garlic, onions, and *[bagoong alamang](:Bagoong_alamang)* (shrimp paste). The name literally means \"wake up, wake up\". It can be eaten alone, on top of rice, or as a [side dish](:Side_dish) to grilled meat dishes. It is a type of *[ginataan](:Ginataan)*."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
