<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mayonnaise> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Mayonnaise** (; ), colloquially referred to as **\"mayo\"** , is a thick, cold, and creamy [sauce](:Sauce) or [dressing](:Salad_dressing) commonly used on [sandwiches](:Sandwich), [hamburgers](:Hamburgers), [composed salads](:Salad%23Bound_salads), and [French fries](:French_fries). It also forms the base for various other sauces, such as [tartar sauce](:Tartar_sauce), [fry sauce](:Fry_sauce), [remoulade](:Remoulade), [salsa golf](:Salsa_golf), and [rouille](:Rouille).Mayonnaise is an [emulsion](:Emulsion) of [oil](:Edible_oil), [egg yolk](:Egg_yolk), and an acid, either [vinegar](:Vinegar) or [lemon juice](:Lemon_juice); there are many variants using additional flavorings. The color varies from near-white to pale yellow, and its texture from a light cream to a thick gel.Commercial eggless imitations are made for those who avoid [chicken eggs](:Chicken_egg) because of [egg allergies](:Egg_allergies), to limit [dietary cholesterol](:Cholesterol), or because they are [vegans](:Veganism)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
