<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bein_mont> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Bein mont** (Template:Lang-my; Template:IPA-my, lit. 'poppy cake') is a Burmese [pancake](:Pancake), widely available as a [street food](:Street_food). It is a traditional Burmese snack, part of a broader family of dishes known as *[mont](:Mont_%28food%29)*. The pancake batter is [rice flour](:Rice_flour) based. After cooking the pancakes are immersed in [jaggery](:Jaggery) syrup with [coconut](:Coconut) shavings and garnished with [sesame](:Sesame) seeds, [peanuts](:Peanut) and [poppy seeds](:Poppy_seed), hence the name."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
