<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tongue_toast> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Tongue toast** is a traditional [open sandwich](:Open_sandwich) prepared with [sauteed](:Saut%C3%A9) [beef tongue](:Beef_tongue) and [scrambled eggs](:Scrambled_eggs). It is seasoned to taste with [black pepper](:Black_pepper) and [onions](:Onion). The tongue is sometimes served on buttered toast with a [poached](:Poaching_%28cooking%29) egg instead of a scrambled one. While it was primarily prepared as a dish for [breakfast](:Breakfast), it was also eaten for [lunch](:Lunch) and [dinner](:Dinner).A variant served for breakfast involved the use of boiled, smoked beef tongue, [cream](:Cream), scrambled egg, and seasoned to taste with [nutmeg](:Nutmeg), [pepper](:Black_pepper), chopped [parsley](:Parsley), and chopped [green peppers](:Bell_pepper). A modern variant involved the use of [reindeer](:Reindeer) tongue instead of beef tongue.Tongue toast was also served as an [hors d'oeuvre](:Hors_d%27oeuvre), prepared in a similar fashion to a [French toast](:French_toast) preparation, as a star-shaped [appetizer](:Appetizer) stamped out of buttered toast with [mustard](:Mustard_%28condiment%29) butter added to it."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
