<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Arenga_pinnata> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Arenga pinnata (syn. Arenga saccharifera) is an economically important feather palm native to tropical Asia, from eastern India east to Malaysia, Indonesia, and the Philippines in the east. Common names include sugar palm, areng palm (also aren palm or arengga palm), black sugar palm, and kaong palm, among other names."@en .
