<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Soufflé> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A **soufflé** is a baked egg-based dish originating in France in the early eighteenth century. Combined with various other ingredients it can be served as a savory main dish or sweetened as a [dessert](:Dessert). The word soufflé is the [past participle](:Past_participle) of the [French](:French_language) [verb](:Verb) *souffler* which means \"to blow\", \"to breathe\", \"to inflate\" or \"to puff\"."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
