<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pusô> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Pusô or tamu, sometimes known in Philippine English as \"hanging rice\", is a Filipino rice cake made by boiling rice in a woven pouch of palm leaves. It is most commonly found in octahedral, diamond, or rectangular shapes, but it can also come in various other intricately woven complex forms. It is known under many different names throughout the Philippines with numerous variations, but it is usually associated with the street food cultures of the Visayan and Moro peoples."@en .
