<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bulgogi> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***Bulgogi*** (불고기;  [*bool-GOH-gee*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key); from [Korean](:Korean_language) *bul-gogi* Template:IPA-ko, literally \"fire meat\", is a *[gui](:Gui_%28food%29)* (구이; Korean-style grilled or roasted dish) made of thin, [marinated](:Marination) slices of meat, most commonly [beef](:Beef), grilled on a barbecue or on a stove-top griddle. It is also often stir-fried in a pan in home cooking. [Sirloin](:Sirloin_steak), [rib eye](:Rib_eye_steak) or [brisket](:Brisket) are frequently used cuts of beef for the dish. The dish originated from northern areas of the Korean Peninsula, but is a very popular dish in [South Korea](:South_Korea), where it can be found anywhere from upscale restaurants to local supermarkets as pan-ready kits."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
