<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Macroom_Oatmeal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Macroom Oatmeal is a traditional stone-ground Irish oatmeal produced in Macroom, County Cork, Ireland, at Walton's Mill, the last surviving stone mill in Ireland. It was taken aboard Slow Food's Ark of Taste in 2011, as of 2019 one of twelve Irish foods selected for the ark."@en .
