<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Blancmange> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Blancmange** (, from Template:Lang-fr Template:IPA-fr is a sweet [dessert](:Dessert) popular throughout [Europe](:Europe) commonly made with [milk](:Milk) or [cream](:Cream) and [sugar](:Sugar) thickened with [rice flour](:Rice_flour), [gelatin](:Gelatin), [corn starch](:Corn_starch), or [Irish moss](:Chondrus_crispus) (a source of [carrageenan](:Carrageenan%29), and often flavoured with [almonds](:Almond).It is usually set in a mould and served cold. Although traditionally white (hence the name, in English literally \"white eating\"), blancmanges are frequently given alternative colours. Some similar desserts are French chef [Marie-Antoine Carême](:Marie-Antoine_Car%C3%AAme)'s [Bavarian cream](:Bavarian_cream), [Italian](:Italian_cuisine) *[panna cotta](:Panna_cotta)*, the [Middle Eastern](:Middle_Eastern_cuisine) *[muhallebi](:Muhallebi)*, [Chinese](:Chinese_cuisine) *[annin tofu](:Annin_tofu),* [Hawai'ian](:Hawai%CA%BBi) *[haupia](:Haupia)* and [Puerto Rican](:Puerto_Rican_cuisine) *[tembleque](:Tembleque)*.The historical blancmange originated at some time during the [Middle Ages](:Middle_Ages) and usually consisted of [capon](:Capon) or [chicken](:Chicken_as_food), milk or [almond milk](:Almond_milk), rice, and sugar and was considered to be ideal for the sick. *[Tavuk göğsü](:Tavuk_g%C3%B6%C4%9Fs%C3%BC)* is a sweet contemporary [Turkish](:Turkish_cuisine) pudding made with shredded chicken, similar to the medieval European dish."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
