<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Fried_pickle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fried pickles, or frickles are a snack food found commonly in the Southern U.S. They are made by deep-frying sliced battered dill pickles. Fried pickles first appeared on the American culinary scene in the early 1960s. The first known fried pickle recipe was printed in the Oakland Tribune on November 19, 1962, for \"French Fried Pickles,\" which called for using sweet pickle slices and pancake mix."@en .
