<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kkakdugi> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Soups & stews*****[Banchan](:Banchan)******[Tteok](:Tteok)******Kkakdugi*** (깍두기) or **diced radish kimchi** is a variety of [kimchi](:Kimchi) in [Korean cuisine](:Korean_cuisine). Usually, [Korean radish](:Korean_radish) (called *mu*, [무](https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/무) in Korean) is used, but other vegetables or fruits can also be used. *Kkakduk-kkakduk* is an [ideophone](:Ideophone) related to dicing/cubing. Kimchi made with radish that are not diced into cubes are not called *kkakdugi*. *Kkakdugi* is a popular [banchan](:Banchan) (side dish) enjoyed by Koreans and others."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
