<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweet_roll> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A **sweet [roll](:Bread_roll)** or **sweet [bun](:Bun)** refers to any of a number of sweet, baked, [yeast](:Baker%27s_yeast)-[leavened](:Leavening_agent) [breakfast](:Breakfast) or [dessert](:Dessert) foods. They may contain [spices](:Spiced_bun), [nuts](:Nut_roll), [candied fruits](:Fruit_bun), etc., and are often [glazed](:Glaze_%28cooking_technique%29) or topped with [icing](:Icing_%28food%29). Compared to regular bread [dough](:Dough), sweet roll dough generally has higher levels of sugar, fat, eggs, and yeast. They are often round, and are small enough to comprise a [single serving](:Serving_size). These differ from [pastries](:Pastries), which are made from a [paste](:Wheatpaste)-like [batter](:Batter_%28cooking%29); from [cakes](:Cake), which are typically unleavened or chemically leavened; and from [doughnuts](:Doughnut), which are [deep fried](:Deep_frying).Refrigerated ready-to-bake sweet roll dough is commercially available in grocery stores.Sweet rolls are sometimes iced and/or contain a sweet filling. In some traditions, other types of fillings and decoration are used, such as cinnamon, [marzipan](:Marzipan), or candied fruit."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
