<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Macroom_Oatmeal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Macroom Oatmeal** is a traditional stone-ground Irish oatmeal produced in [Macroom](:Macroom), County Cork, Ireland, at Walton's Mill, the last surviving stone mill in Ireland. It was taken aboard [Slow Food](:Slow_Food)'s [Ark of Taste](:Ark_of_Taste) in 2011, as of 2019 one of twelve Irish foods selected for the ark."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
