<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Flatbread> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A **flatbread** is a [bread](:Bread) made with [flour](:Flour); [water](:Water), [milk](:Milk), [yogurt](:Yogurt), or other liquid; and [salt](:Salt), and then thoroughly rolled into flattened [dough](:Dough). Many flatbreads are [unleavened](:Unleavened_bread), although some are leavened, such as [pizza](:Pizza) and [pita bread](:Pita_bread).Flatbreads range from below one millimeter to a few centimeters thick so that they can be easily eaten without being sliced. They can be baked in an oven, fried in hot oil, grilled over hot coals, cooked on a hot pan, [tava](:Tava), [comal](:Comal_%28cookware%29), or metal griddle, and eaten fresh or packaged and frozen for later use."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
