<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Shahe_fen> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***Shahe fen*** (沙河粉), or simply ***he fen*** (河粉), is a type of wide [Chinese noodle](:Chinese_noodle) made from [rice](:Rice). Its [Minnan Chinese](:Min_Nan) name, translated from the Mandarin 粿條 (***guotiao***), is adapted into alternate names which are widely encountered in [Southeast Asia](:Southeast_Asia), such as ***kway teow***, ***kwetiau***, and ***kuetiau***. *Shahe fen* is often [stir fried](:Stir_frying) with meat and/or vegetables in a dish called ***chao fen*** (炒粉; pinyin: chǎo fěn). While *chao fen* is a transliteration of [Mandarin](:Mandarin_Chinese), ***chow fun*** from [Cantonese](:Cantonese_Language) (see the main article at [beef chow fun](:Beef_chow_fun%29) is the name most often given to the dish in [Chinese restaurants in North America](:American_Chinese_cuisine)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
