<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Porridge> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Porridge** is a food made by heating or boiling ground, crushed or chopped starchy plants, typically grain, in milk or water. It is often cooked or served with added flavourings such as sugar, honey, (dried) fruit or syrup to make a sweet cereal, or it can be mixed with spices, meat or vegetables to make a [savoury](:Savoury_%28dish%29) dish. It is usually served hot in a bowl, depending on its consistency. Oat porridge, or [oatmeal](:Oatmeal), is one of the most common types of porridge. [Gruel](:Gruel) is a thinner version of porridge."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
