<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Obwarzanek_krakowski> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An ****obwarzanek krakowski**** (Template:IPA-pl, plural: **obwarzanki krakowskie** Template:IPA-pl; also spelled **obarzanek**) is a braided ring-shaped [bread](:Bread) that is boiled and sprinkled with [salt](:Salt) and [sesame](:Sesame) or [poppy seeds](:Poppy_seed) before being baked. It has a white, sweetish, moist and chewy crumb underneath a crunchy golden-brown crust. Traditionally sold from street carts, it is a popular snack in the Polish city of [Kraków](:Krak%C3%B3w), where it has the status of a regional food with [protected geographical indication](:Protected_geographical_indication). It is closely related to, but distinct from, [bagels](:Bagel), [bubliks](:Bublik) and [pretzels](:Pretzels)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
