<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Huangjiu> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Huangjiu (Chinese: 黄酒), meaning yellow wine, is a Chinese alcoholic beverage, and is most popular in the Jiangnan area. Huangjiu is brewed by mixing boiled grains including rice, glutinous rice or millet with qū as starter culture, followed by saccharification and fermentation at around 13-18 °C for fortnights. Its alcohol content is typically 8%-20%."@en .
