<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Soy_sauce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Soy sauce** (also called simply **soy** in [American English](:American_English) and **soya sauce** in [British English](:British_English%29) is a liquid [condiment](:Condiment) of Chinese origin, traditionally made from a [fermented](:Fermentation_%28food%29) paste of [soybeans](:Soybean), roasted [grain](:Cereal), [brine](:Brine), and *[Aspergillus oryzae](:Aspergillus_oryzae)* or *[Aspergillus sojae](:Aspergillus_sojae)* [molds](:Mold_%28fungus%29). It is considered to contain a strong [umami](:Umami) taste.Soy sauce in its current form was created about 2,200 years ago during the [Western Han dynasty](:Han_dynasty%23Western_Han) of ancient China, and it has spread throughout East and [Southeast Asia](:Southeast_Asia) where it is used in cooking and as a condiment."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
