<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tubaani> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Tubaani** also referred to as *steamed black-eyed peas' pudding* is a popular [Ghanaian dish](:Ghanaian_cuisine) that is commonly eaten in the northern regions and [Zongo](:Zongo_settlements) communities of [Ghana](:Ghana). The dish consists of a paste made from the flour of [black-eyed peas](:Black-eyed_pea) and water which is then cooked after being first wrapped in the sweet-tasting, aromatic leaves of the [Marantaceous](:Marantaceae) herb [Thaumatococcus daniellii](:Thaumatococcus_daniellii) and served with gravy or pepper and sliced onions tossed in hot vegetable oil."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
