<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pickled_cucumber> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A **pickled cucumber** (commonly known as a **pickle** in the United States and Canada, and a **gherkin** in Britain, Ireland, South Africa, Australia, and New Zealand) is a small or miniature [cucumber](:Cucumber) that has been [pickled](:Pickling) in a [brine](:Brine_%28food%29), [vinegar](:Vinegar), or other solution and left to ferment for some time, by either immersing the cucumbers in an acidic solution or through [souring](:Souring) by [lacto-fermentation](:Lacto-fermentation). Pickled cucumbers are often part of [mixed pickles](:Mixed_pickles)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
