<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kamarcut> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Kamarcut** is a traditional [South Indian](:South_India) [candy](:Candy) made out of [jaggery](:Jaggery) and is made by slowly cooking jaggery with [water](:Water) until it achieves a [honeylike](:Honey) consistency. Shredded [coconut](:Coconut) can be added to the mixture to create texture.It used to be available widely in South India but has become harder to obtain in urban areas. It is still often sold in villages, but is still hard to obtain."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
