<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Rock_candy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Rock candy** or **[sugar](:Sugar) candy**, also called **rock sugar**, or **crystal sugar**, is a type of [confection](:Confection) composed of relatively large sugar [crystals](:Crystal). This candy is formed by allowing a [supersaturated](:Supersaturation) solution of sugar and water to crystallize onto a surface suitable for crystal [nucleation](:Nucleation), such as a string, stick, or plain granulated sugar. Heating the water before adding the sugar allows more sugar to dissolve thus producing larger crystals. Crystals form after 6 to 7 days. [Food coloring](:Food_coloring) may be added to the mixture to produce colored candy."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
