<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dessert> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Dessert** is a [course](:Course_%28food%29) that concludes a meal. The course consists of sweet foods, such as [confections](:Confections), and possibly a beverage such as [dessert wine](:Dessert_wine) and [liqueur](:Liqueur). In some parts of the world, such as much of [Greece](:Greece) and [West Africa](:West_Africa), and most parts of [China](:China), there is no tradition of a dessert course to conclude a meal.The term *dessert* can apply to many [confections](:Confectionery), such as [biscuits](:Biscuit), [cakes](:Cake), [cookies](:Cookie), [custards](:Custard), [gelatins](:Gelatin_dessert), [ice creams](:Ice_cream), [pastries](:Pastry), [pies](:Pie), [puddings](:Pudding), [macaroons](:Macaroon), [sweet soups](:Tong_sui), [tarts](:Tart), and [fruit salad](:Fruit_salad). [Fruit](:Fruit) is also commonly found in dessert courses because of its naturally occurring sweetness. Some cultures sweeten foods that are more commonly [savory](:Umami) to create desserts."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
