<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Knödel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Knödel** (Template:IPA-de; sing. and pl.) or **Klöße** (Template:IPA-de; sing. *Kloß*) are [boiled](:Boiling) [dumplings](:Dumpling) commonly found in [Central European](:Central_European_cuisine) and [East European cuisine](:East_European_cuisine). Central European countries in which their variant of *Knödel* is popular include Austria, Germany, Hungary, Poland, Romania, Bosnia, Croatia, Serbia, Slovenia, Slovakia, Bulgaria and Czechia. They are also found in [Scandinavian](:Scandinavia), [Romanian](:Romanian_cuisine), [northeastern Italian cuisine](:Italian_cuisine%23Trentino-Alto_Adige), [Ukrainian](:Ukrainian_cuisine) and [Belarusian](:Belarusian_cuisine) cuisines. Usually made from [flour](:Flour), [bread](:Bread) or [potatoes](:Potato), they are often served as a [side dish](:Side_dish), but can also be a [dessert](:Dessert) such as [plum dumplings](:Plum_Dumplings), or even [meat balls](:Leberkn%C3%B6del) in soup. Many varieties and variations exist."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
