<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Meze> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Meze or mezze (/ˈmɛzeɪ/, /ˈmɛzɛ/) is a selection of small dishes served as appetizers in much of West Asia, Middle East and the Balkans. Meze is often served as a part of multi-course meals. They are popular in the Levant, Iran, Greece, Turkey, the Caucasus and the Balkans."@en .
