<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sambal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Sambal** is an [Indonesian](:Bumbu_%28seasoning%29) [chilli sauce](:Chilli_sauce) or [paste](:Chili_paste), typically made from a mixture of a variety of [chilli peppers](:Chilli_pepper) with secondary ingredients, such as [shrimp paste](:Shrimp_paste), [garlic](:Garlic), [ginger](:Ginger), [shallot](:Shallot), [scallion](:Scallion), [palm sugar](:Palm_sugar), and [lime juice](:Lime_juice). *Sambal* is an [Indonesian](:Indonesian_language) [loan-word](:Loan-word) of [Javanese](:Javanese_language) origin (*sambel*). It originated from [the culinary traditions of Indonesia](:Indonesian_cuisine), and is also an integral part of the cuisines of [Malaysia](:Malaysian_cuisine), [Sri Lanka](:Sri_Lankan_cuisine), [Brunei](:Bruneian_cuisine) and [Singapore](:Singaporean_cuisine). It has also spread through [overseas Indonesian populations](:Overseas_Indonesians) to the [Netherlands](:Netherlands) and [Suriname](:Suriname).Various recipes of *sambals* usually are served as hot and spicy [condiments](:Condiments) for dishes, such as *[lalab](:Lalab)* (raw vegetables), *[ikan bakar](:Ikan_bakar)* (grilled fish), *[ikan goreng](:Ikan_goreng)* (fried fish), *[ayam goreng](:Ayam_goreng)* (fried chicken), *[ayam penyet](:Ayam_penyet)* (smashed chicken), *[iga penyet](:Iga_penyet)* (ribs) and various *[soto](:Soto_%28food%29)* soup. There are 212 variants of sambal in Indonesia, with most of them originating from [Java](:Java)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
