<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Polenta> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Polenta** (, Template:IPA-it is a dish of boiled [cornmeal](:Cornmeal) that was historically made from other grains. The dish comes from [Italy](:Italy). It may be served as a hot [porridge](:Porridge), or it may be allowed to cool and solidify into a loaf that can be baked, fried, or [grilled](:Grilling).The variety of cereal used is usually yellow [maize](:Maize), but often [buckwheat](:Buckwheat), white maize, or mixtures thereof may be used. Coarse grinds make a firm, coarse polenta; finer grinds make a soft, creamy polenta. Polenta is a staple of [Northern Italian](:Northern_Italian_cuisine), [Swiss](:Swiss_cuisine) and [Balkan](:Balkan_cuisine) (where it is called [kačamak](:Ka%C4%8Damak) or [žganci](:%C5%BDganci%29) cuisines (and, to a lesser extent, the Central Italian one, e.g. [Tuscany](:Tuscan_cuisine%29) and its consumption was traditionally associated with lower classes, as in times past [cornmeal mush](:Mush_%28cornmeal%29) was an essential food in their everyday nutrition."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
