<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kabanos> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Kabanos** (; plural: *kabanosy*), also known as **cabanossi** or **kabana**, is a long, thin, [dry sausage](:Dry_sausage) usually made of [pork](:Pork) which originated in [Poland](:Poland). They are smoky in flavor, and can be soft or very dry in texture depending on freshness. Typically, they are quite long, 60 cm (24 in), but very thin, with a diameter around 1 cm (0.39 in), and folded in two, giving them a characteristic appearance. Versions made of [chicken](:Chicken_%28food%29) and [turkey](:Turkey_meat) are staples in [kosher](:Kosher) meat markets and [delicatessens](:Delicatessens)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
