<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Meze> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Meze** or **mezza** (, ) is a selection of small dishes served as appetizers in the [Levant](:Levantine_cuisine), [Turkey](:Turkish_cuisine), [Greece](:Greek_cuisine), the [Balkans](:Balkan_cuisine), the [Caucasus](:Caucasian_cuisine), and [Iran](:Iranian_cuisine). It is similar to [Spanish](:Spanish_cuisine) [tapas](:Tapas) and [Italian](:Italian_cuisine) [antipasti](:Antipasto). A mezze may be served as a part of a multi-course meal or form a meal in itself. Mezze are often served with alcoholic beverages such as [arak](:Arak_%28drink%29)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
