<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Salad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A **salad** is a [dish](:Dish_%28food%29) consisting of mixed, mostly natural ingredients with at least one raw ingredient. They are often dressed, and typically served at room temperature or chilled, though some can be served warm.**Garden salads** use a base of [leafy greens](:Leaf_vegetable) such as [lettuce](:Lettuce), [arugula/rocket](:Eruca_sativa), [kale](:Kale) or [spinach](:Spinach); they are common enough that the word *salad* alone often refers specifically to garden salads. Other types include [bean salad](:Bean_salad), [tuna salad](:Tuna_salad), bread salad (e.g. [fattoush](:Fattoush), [panzanella](:Panzanella%29), vegetable salads without leafy greens (e.g. [Greek salad](:Greek_salad), [potato salad](:Potato_salad), [coleslaw](:Coleslaw%29), [sōmen salad](:S%C5%8Dmen_salad) (a noodle-based salad), [fruit salad](:Fruit_salad), and desserts like [jello salad](:Jello_salad).Salads may be served at any point during a meal:When a sauce is used to flavor a salad, it is generally called a [salad dressing](:Salad_dressing); most salad dressings are based on either [a mixture of oil and vinegar](:Vinaigrette) or a creamy dairy base."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
