<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chip_butty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A **chip butty** is a [sandwich](:Sandwich) filled with chips (thick-cut deep fried potatoes, similar to [steak fries](:Steak_fries%29), optionally eaten with condiments such as [brown sauce](:Brown_sauce), [ketchup](:Ketchup), [mayonnaise](:Mayonnaise), or [malt vinegar](:Malt_vinegar). The bread may be slices from a loaf or a bread roll, and is usually buttered. The chip butty can be found in [fish and chip shops](:Fish_and_chip_shop) and other [casual dining](:Casual_dining) establishments in the [British Isles](:British_Isles).Other names for the sandwich may relate to the variety of bread used, such as chip roll or chip muffin, or a [regional type of bread roll](:List_of_bread_rolls) such as chip bap, chip cob or chip [barm](:Barm_cake)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
