<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Yaksik> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***Yaksik*** or ***yakbap*** (literally \"medicinal food\" or \"medicinal rice\") is a sweet [Korean](:Korea_cuisine) dish made by steaming [glutinous rice](:Glutinous_rice), and mixing with [chestnuts](:Chestnuts), [jujubes](:Jujube), and [pine nuts](:Pine_nut). It is seasoned with [honey](:Honey) or [brown sugar](:Brown_sugar), [sesame oil](:Sesame_oil), [soy sauce](:Soy_sauce), and sometimes [cinnamon](:Cinnamomum_cassia). It is traditionally eaten on [Jeongwol Daeboreum](:Jeongwol_Daeboreum) (정월대보름), a Korean holiday which falls on every January 15 in the [lunar calendar](:Lunar_calendar), but also for weddings and [hwangap](:Hwangap) festivities."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
