<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bread_roll> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A roll is a small, usually round or oblong individual loaf of bread served as a meal accompaniment (eaten plain or with butter). Rolls can be served and eaten whole or are also commonly cut and filled – the result of doing so is considered a sandwich in American English and in Britain."@en .
