<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lombardy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Lombardy (Lombard and Italian: Lombardia) is one of the twenty administrative regions of Italy. It has an extent of 23,844 km2 (9,206 sq mi) in the northern-central part of the country, and a population of about 10 million people, constituting more than one-sixth of the population of Italy. Over a fifth of the Italian gross domestic product is produced in the region."@en .
