<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Spaghetti> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Spaghetti** (Template:IPA-it is a long, thin, solid, cylindrical [pasta](:Pasta). It is a [staple food](:Staple_food) of traditional [Italian cuisine](:Italian_cuisine). Like other pasta, spaghetti is made of [milled](:Milling_%28grinding%29) [wheat](:Wheat) and [water](:Water) and sometimes [enriched](:Enriched_flour) with vitamins and minerals. Italian spaghetti is typically made from [durum](:Durum) wheat [semolina](:Semolina). Usually the pasta is white because refined flour is used, but whole wheat flour may be added. *Spaghettoni* is a thicker form of spaghetti, while *[capellini](:Capellini)* is a very thin spaghetti.Originally, spaghetti was notably long, but shorter lengths gained in popularity during the latter half of the 20th century and now it is most commonly available in 25–30 cm (10–12 in) lengths. A variety of pasta [dishes](:Dish_%28food%29) are based on it and it is frequently served with [tomato sauce](:Tomato_sauce) or meat or vegetables."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
