<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Apfelwein> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Apfelwein ([ˈʔapfl̩vaɪn] German, 'apple wine'), or Viez ([fiːts] Moselfranken, Saarland, Trier, vice) or Most ([mɔst] Austria, Switzerland, South Germany, must) are German words for cider. It is made from a mix of sour tasting apples, such as \"Bohnapfel\" or \"Speierling\", respectively. It has an alcohol content of 4.8–7.0% and a tart, sour taste."@en .
