<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Masa_podrida> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***Masa podrida*** are traditional [Filipino](:Filipino_cuisine) [shortbread cookies](:Shortbread_cookie) made from flour, salt, baking powder, brown sugar, shortening, and eggs. It has a dry crumbly texture similar to [half-moon cookies](:Half-moon_cookie_%28Filipino%29). The name comes from [Spanish](:Spanish_language) for \"rotten dough\". *Masa podrida* are typically eaten with coffee and other hot drinks."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
