<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hangwa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Soups & stews*****[Banchan](:Banchan)******[Tteok](:Tteok)******Hangwa*** (한과; 韓菓) is a general term for traditional Korean [confections](:Confectionery). With *[tteok](:Tteok)* (rice cakes), *hangwa* forms the sweet food category in [Korean cuisine](:Korean_cuisine). Common ingredients of *hangwa* include [grain](:Grain) [flour](:Flour), [fruits](:Fruit) and [roots](:Edible_root), sweet ingredients such as [honey](:Honey) and *[yeot](:Yeot)*, and spices such as [cinnamon](:Cinnamomum_cassia) and [ginger](:Ginger)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
