<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dumpling> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Dumpling** is a broad class of dishes that consist of pieces of [dough](:Dough) (made from a variety of [starch](:Starch) sources), often wrapped around a filling. The dough can be based on [bread](:Bread), [flour](:Flour), [buckwheat](:Buckwheat) or [potatoes](:Potato), and may be filled with [meat](:Meat), [fish](:Fish_%28food%29), [tofu](:Tofu), [cheese](:Cheese), [vegetables](:Vegetable), [fruits](:Fruit) or [sweets](:Sweets). Dumplings may be prepared using a variety of methods, including [baking](:Baking), [boiling](:Boiling), [frying](:Frying), [simmering](:Simmering) or [steaming](:Steaming) and are found in many world cuisines. In the [United States](:United_States_of_America) in May 2015 [National Day Calendar](:Marlo_Anderson) listed National Dumpling Day as held on September 26, annually."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
