<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kalamay> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***Kalamay*** (also spelled ***Calamay***, literally \"sugar\"), is a sticky sweet delicacy that is popular in many regions of the [Philippines](:Philippines). It is made of [coconut milk](:Coconut_milk), [brown sugar](:Brown_sugar), and ground [glutinous rice](:Glutinous_rice). It can also be flavored with [margarine](:Margarine), [peanut butter](:Peanut_butter), or [vanilla](:Vanilla). *Kalamay* can be eaten alone but is usually used as a sweetener for a number of [Filipino](:Filipino_people) [desserts](:Dessert) and beverages. It is related to the [Chamorro](:Chamorro_people) dessert called [Kalamai](:Kalamai_%28dessert%29)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
