<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Onion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The onion (Allium cepa L., from Latin cepa meaning \"onion\"), also known as the bulb onion or common onion, is a vegetable that is the most widely cultivated species of the genus Allium. The shallot is a botanical variety of the onion which was classified as a separate species until 2010. Its close relatives include garlic, scallion, leek, and chive."@en .
