<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bamia> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Bamia** is a Middle Eastern, Armenian, Afghan, Kurdish, Anatolian and Turkish [stew](:Stew) prepared using [lamb](:Lamb_and_mutton), [okra](:Okra) and tomatoes as primary ingredients. Additional ingredients used include tomato sauce, onion, garlic, [cilantro](:Cilantro) (coriander), vegetable oil, [cardamom](:Cardamom), salt and pepper. The word \"bamia\" itself simply means \"[okra](:Okra)\" and it is [etymologically](:Etymology) an Arabic word.Vegetarian bamia is very popular during fasting seasons such as [Easter](:Easter) in [Greece](:Greece) and [Cyprus](:Cyprus)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
