<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ogwa-cha> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***Ogwa-cha*** (오과차; 五果茶) or **five fruit tea** is a [traditional Korean tea](:Traditional_Korean_tea) made with [walnut](:Walnut), [ginkgo](:Ginkgo), [jujube](:Jujube), [chestnut](:Castanea_crenata), and *[gotgam](:Gotgam)* (dried [persimmon](:Diospyros_kaki%29). The ingredients are mashed with [ginger](:Ginger), boiled in water, and strained to make the tea. Optionally, honey can be added to taste."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
