<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kinutil> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Kinutil**, also known as **kinutir** or **kutir**, is a [Filipino](:Filipino_cuisine) [alcoholic drink](:Alcoholic_drink) from the [Visayas Islands](:Visayas_Islands) and [Mindanao](:Mindanao). It is made from palm wine ([tubâ](:Tub%C3%A2%29) with raw [egg yolks](:Egg_yolk) and/or homemade chocolate (*[tabliya](:Tabliya)*). Some versions also add [condensed milk](:Condensed_milk), sugar, and carbonated [softdrinks](:Softdrink). A version made with chocolate and sugar in the island of [Samar](:Samar) is known as **dubado**. It is typically paired with Filipino rice cakes (*[kakanin](:Kakanin)*). The name means \"stirred\", from [Visayan](:Visayan_languages) *kutil* (\"to stir\"). It is sometimes characterized as the \"Filipino [eggnog](:Eggnog)\" or the \"Filipino mudslide\"."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
