<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dried_and_salted_cod> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Dried and salted cod, sometimes referred to as salt cod or saltfish or salt dolly, is cod which has been preserved by drying after salting. Cod which has been dried without the addition of salt is stockfish. Salt cod was long a major export of the North Atlantic region, and has become an ingredient of many cuisines around the Atlantic and in the Mediterranean."@en .
