<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pretzel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A pretzel, from German pronunciation, standard German: Breze(l) ( and French / Alsatian: Bretzel) is a type of baked bread made from dough that is commonly shaped into a knot. The traditional pretzel shape is a distinctive symmetrical form, with the ends of a long strip of dough intertwined and then twisted back onto itself in a particular way (a pretzel loop or pretzel bow). Today, pretzels come in a wide range of shapes."@en .
