<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pastil> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "***Pastil***, or ***pastel***, is a [Filipino](:Philippine_cuisine) packed [rice](:Rice) dish made with [steamed rice](:Steamed_rice) wrapped in [banana leaves](:Banana_leaves) with dry shredded [beef](:Beef), [chicken](:Chicken_as_food), or [fish](:Fish_as_food). It originates from the [Maguindanao people](:Maguindanao_people) and is a popular, cheap breakfast meal in [Mindanao](:Mindanao), especially among [Muslim Filipinos](:Muslim_Filipinos). *Pastil* is also known as *patil*, *patel*, *patir*, or *pater* in [Maranao](:Maranao_language); and *paster* in [Iranun](:Iranun_language).Pastil is also the [Tausūg](:Taus%C5%ABg_people) name for a type of [empanada](:Empanada), an unrelated pastry made with beansprout and glass noodle fillings mostly popular in Zamboanga City."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
